<metadata_system id="160" name="Android MediaStore Metadata" category="IMG" category_label="Images" used_for="Android phone/tablet media library — MediaStore content provider" spec_source="Android Open Source Project — android.provider.MediaStore + MediaColumns" completeness="comprehensive" record_count="92">
  <description>Android's MediaStore is a content provider that indexes all media files (images, videos, audio, documents, downloads) on a device's storage. Apps query MediaStore via content URIs to access the media library without dealing with raw filesystem paths (especially after scoped storage in Android 10+). MediaStore wraps a SQLite database (external.db) that stores per-file metadata: dimensions, duration, capture date, mime type, owner package, edit history, favorite/trash state, EXIF-derived date/orientation, etc. This entry covers the full column catalog across BaseColumns, MediaColumns, Images.Media, Video.Media, Audio.Media, Files.FileColumns, Downloads, and provider-level URIs and permissions.</description>
